# Data Card — Multi-Plant Order Allocation

## Name and version
Synthetic data pack v1.0 — 2026-10-11

## How it was made
Generated synthetically using Python scripts with seed=42.
No real company or personal data used.

## What it contains
| Table | Rows | Date Range |
|-------|------|------------|
| orders.csv | 150 | 2026-10-12 to 2026-11-30 |
| plants.csv | 90 (3 plants × 5 products × 6 weeks) | 2026-10-12 to 2026-11-30 |
| transport_duties.csv | 36 (3 plants × 12 destinations) | — |
| capacity_events.csv | 3 | 2026-10-19 to 2026-11-29 |

## Traps and edge cases
- ORD-007: cheapest plant (A) arrives late; must use B or C
- P5 orders: only Plant C can make them
- Chicago duty: A=25%, B=6%, C=0% — flips cheapest plant
- Plant C: lowest carbon (0.2) but only 400 units/week
- E002: Plant C loses 85% capacity → P5 orders infeasible
- Carbon intensity changes weekly (0.17–0.31)

## Checks run
All 5 validation checks pass (see scripts/validate_data.py).

## Known limits
- No real-world variability in transit
- No currency fluctuation
- No supplier constraints

## Privacy
No real company or personal data included.